 "id": "01a10bd8-c209-7333-a5c6-148746b63f6a",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (changed late Sep/Oct 2026 when Finance moved to a new accounting tool): plain comma-separated (`,`), dates ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, UTF-8 without a BOM. The earlier German-locale format (`;` delimiter, `DD.MM.YYYY`) is obsolete.",
 "summary": "Monthly export: consumer and contents; now comma-separated with ISO dates",
 "premise": "while Finance uses the new accounting tool that wants comma-separated files and ISO dates",
